{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>A Psalm of David, when he fled.</b> The Gaon [Saadia] wished to connect all the psalms one to the next, and said: after \"the nations raged\" — for the like of what happened with Absalom can happen to them. But the commentator has no ability to connect thus. And this psalm is written in the first book, for there are five books; therefore one should not be surprised if we find in the fifth \"A prayer, when he was in the cave,\" which was before the affair of Absalom, and a psalm by way of prophecy, that he prophesied he would prevail — upon which \"He answered me from His holy hill, a swift response,\" like the prayer of Jonah: \"and my prayer came to You.\""], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:00.014019795Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}